.TH DIGINET-PACKET-HELPER 1 2026-10-29 "libdiginet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diginet-packet-helper \- open the DigiNet packet socket for an unprivileged program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diginet-packet-helper
.B 3<>
.I connected-unix-socket
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diginet-packet-helper
opens one raw packet socket for EtherType 0x885F, the protocol of the Digidesign Control|24 and
ProControl, bound to no interface, so that it hears a desk on every network interface,
interfaces that come up later included. It passes that socket over its descriptor 3, which must
be a connected
.B AF_UNIX
socket, with
.BR SCM_RIGHTS ,
and exits.
.PP
It exists so that the program that drives the desk needs no privilege. Opening a packet socket
needs the
.B cap_net_raw
capability; using one that is already open does not. The helper holds the capability, the
program starts it, takes the socket and keeps no capability of its own. The library does all of
it in one call,
.BR diginet_packet_open_by_helper (),
declared in
.IR <diginet/transport/diginet_io.h> :
a socketpair, the helper started with one end on its descriptor 3 and an empty environment,
.BR diginet_packet_receive_fd (),
which takes only an
.B AF_PACKET
socket, and the wait for the helper to exit.
.PP
The helper takes no arguments, reads no file, no environment and no input, loops on nothing and
keeps no descriptor. The socket it passes carries only EtherType 0x885F, on every interface.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The socket was passed.
.TP
.B 1
The helper does not hold
.BR cap_net_raw ;
it says "needs cap_net_raw" on standard error.
.TP
.B 2
Descriptor 3 is not a connected Unix socket, an argument was given, or the socket could not be
opened or passed; standard error says which.
.SH FILES
The packages install it with the one capability it needs, as
.PP
.RS
setcap cap_net_raw=ep /usr/bin/diginet-packet-helper
.RE
.PP
and check it with
.BR getcap (8),
because
.BR install (1)
and every rebuild make a binary without it. It is linked statically against libdiginet, so it
loads no shared library of the project while it holds the capability.
.SH SECURITY
Any user who may run the helper gets a raw socket for EtherType 0x885F on every interface: one
that can hear and send DigiNet frames, and nothing else. A site that wants fewer users to have
that restricts who may run it, for example with a group of its own and mode 0750.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diginet-probe (1),
.BR packet (7),
.BR unix (7),
.BR capabilities (7),
.BR setcap (8),
.BR getcap (8)
